<!--
    The select-text mark, from Material Symbols' `text_select_start` (outlined).

    An I-beam caret with the selection's extent beside it: the gesture the menu's row
    opens — pick characters out of this message's own source — drawn as the set draws it.

    ## Provenance

    Google's Material Symbols,
    `symbols/web/text_select_start/materialsymbolsoutlined/text_select_start_24px.svg`,
    Apache-2.0. The `d` attribute below is that file's own, character for character.

    The one mechanical edit is the viewport, not the path: a Symbols SVG is authored on
    `viewBox="0 0 -960 960 960"` — the y axis runs *upwards* from -960 — and an Android
    vector has no origin offset, so the figure is moved down by the whole viewport in a
    `<group android:translateY="960">` rather than by rewriting any coordinate. Moving a
    path by arithmetic is how `ic_copy.xml`'s back sheet ended up 85.333 units too high;
    a group asks the renderer to do the same addition, and the numbers stay Google's.
    (`translateY`, not the `translationY` of a layout modifier: a vector group's own
    attributes are floats on the viewport's grid, and the dimension attribute AAPT binds
    that name to is rejected — `'960' is incompatible with attribute translationY`.)

    ## The name that was asked for, and does not exist

    The request was `format_select_text`. There is no such glyph: the variable font's own
    codepoints file lists 4304 names and none of them is that, the classic Material Icons
    metadata's 2122 do not have it either, and Iconify's `material-symbols` collection
    answers `not_found` for the same string. The set's own vocabulary for this idea is
    the `text_select_*` family, and `text_select_start` is the one that means "begin
    selecting text" — see ARCHITECTURE §12.3 for the candidates that were rendered at
    21dp before this one was chosen.
-->
